Reply to a libfabric handshake that re-establishes a known connection.

NIXL 1.5.0's libfabric backend sends a handshake only from the side that
creates a fresh connection, and a handshake for a connection the receiver
already holds only marks it received. So when one agent invalidates a live
peer and loads it again, its new connection sends a handshake that the
peer, which kept its own connection, never answers. Every post to that
peer then waits NIXL_LIBFABRIC_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_S (60 s) and fails with
NIXL_ERR_REMOTE_DISCONNECT. A dKV connector that evicts a peer over its
table cap and attaches it again hits this (CLIN-2277).

A handshake that carries the sender's connection info (has_conn=1) says
the sender has not seen our handshake. The receiver now answers it with a
has_conn=0 handshake, which cannot loop. When the progress thread owns the
rails, the reply goes through the connection-management thread, so it is
never posted from the progress thread's completion context. The wire
format does not change, so a patched agent interoperates with an unpatched
one. The fix takes effect on the side that kept its connection.

This is a backport of ai-dynamo/nixl#2438, merged upstream as 9426653281
after v1.5.0; no tagged release carries it through v1.5.2. The diff is
that commit's src/ changes, with only the trailing space on blank context
lines stripped by the repo's pre-commit hook. Its unit tests and CI script
are left out.

TODO(CLIN-2277): drop once the fix ships in a tagged NIXL release.

